    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nUnified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` field formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (drives the generated `OwnerDto`)\n- Replaced the `customerCode` schema property with `memberId`, documenting the `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` format.\n- Removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` properties.\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- Replaced the `customer_code` column/field (and its getter/setter) with `member_id` / `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`.\n- Removed the `membershipNumber` field and its accessors.\n- Removed the derived `getCheckDigit()` method (its Luhn digit now lives inside `memberId`).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Removed the explicit `checkDigit` mapping; `memberId` now auto-maps by name.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Replaced `assignCustomerCode` with `assignMemberId`, which builds `REGION + FY(2-digit) + HASH8(8 upper-hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)) + Luhn(REGION+FY+HASH8)`, with collision de-duplication now applied to `memberId`.\n- Removed `assignMembershipNumber`; added a `luhnCheckDigit` helper.\n- Updated `primaryIdentifier` to return `getMemberId()`, so the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event carries the `memberId` (under a `memberId` key), and updated the human-readable audit line to log `memberId`.\n\n**Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`)\n- Replaced the `customer_code` column with `member_id` and dropped `membership_number`.\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 68, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS`. Generated ids look like `NSW277D0C08EF9` (NSW + FY27 + 8 hex + check digit).",
